[00:06.13]I remember the feeling,
[00:08.28]warm but uneasy,
[00:10.42]new home, new city,
[00:12.98]low self-esteem.
[00:14.84]I took pill after pill
[00:31.29]just to quiet my head,
[00:45.53]then smoked by the window
[00:49.72]and stayed in my bed.
[00:56.44]Dropped acid alone while
[01:02.87]the ceiling turned strange
[01:06.79]and waited for something
[01:13.91]inside me to change.
[01:21.47]My dealer knew
[01:22.82]when I needed a spark,
[01:26.13]and I called that friendship
[01:28.89]because it was enough.
[01:42.37]At sixteen, I thought
[01:52.72]I had years left to lose.
[01:55.14]At seventeen,
[01:55.50]I had habits to choose.
[01:59.69]I don't miss the fear
[02:01.93]or the things I went through.
[02:04.11]I miss being young enough
[02:06.41]not to know what they'd do.
[02:11.94]My first love came
[02:13.86]through that apartment door.
[02:16.67]I had never let anyone
[02:19.01]that close before.
[03:05.94]I kept the opioids
[03:44.01]hidden where nobody would see,
[03:46.23]took more than I intended
[03:48.84]and kept it all with me.
[03:50.60]I overdosed in silence
[03:53.14]with the bedroom door shut tight,
[03:55.60]then woke up hours later
[03:57.56]and said that I was alright.
[04:00.08]I didn't know what was wrong
[04:02.26]or why I hated my skin.
[04:04.48]I only knew the pills could cut
[04:06.50]the pressure down within.
[04:28.33]I don't call it good,
[04:53.28]and I don't call it bad.
[04:55.36]It held some of the worst
[04:57.52]and the best that I had.
[04:59.63]Now when I remember,
[05:02.15]I can't make it clean.
[05:03.95]I hated those years,
[05:05.95]but I still miss sixteen.
[05:08.09]Newark is traffic
[05:10.41]I pass on the way,
[05:12.53]but part of me stays
[05:14.52]in that bedroom some days.
[05:26.16]I wasn't chasing
[05:27.82]a story to tell.
[05:30.42]I don't miss that bedroom,
[05:49.10]at least not completely,
[05:55.53]but sometimes I miss
[05:58.24]what it meant to be sixteen.
[06:06.69]I remember the feeling,
[06:11.30]warm but uneasy,
[06:12.32]a new home, a new city,
[06:14.36]a life in between.
